,"seed":761386020477757285,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to find how many whole numbers less than \\(18,632\\) are congruent to \\(23 \\pmod{37}\\).\n\nFirst, let's understand what it means for a number \\(n\\) to be congruent to \\(23 \\pmod{37}\\). This means:\n\\[ n = 37k + 23 \\]\nfor some integer \\(k\\). We need \\(n\\) to be less than \\(18,632\\):\n\\[ 37k + 23 < 18,632 \\]\n\nSubtract 23 from both sides:\n\\[ 37k < 18,609 \\]\n\nNext, divide both sides by 37 to solve for \\(k\\):\n\\[ k < \\frac{18,609}{37} \\]\n\nPerform the division:\n\\[ \\frac{18,609}{37} \\approx 502.9459 \\]\n\nSince \\(k\\) must be an integer, we take the floor of \\(502.9459\\):\n\\[ k \\leq 502 \\]\n\nThus, \\(k\\) can take any integer value from \\(0\\) to \\(502\\). This gives us a total of:\n\\[ 502 - 0 + 1 = 503 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of whole numbers less than \\(18,632\\) that are congruent to \\(23 \\pmod{37}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{503}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{503}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
